@startuml Facade Pattern
!theme plain

title Facade Pattern

class SubSystem1 {
    +MethodA(): void
    +MethodB(): void
}

class SubSystem2 {
    +MethodA(): void
    +MethodB(): void
}

class SubSystem3 {
    +MethodA(): void
    +MethodB(): void
}

class Facade {
    -subSystem1: SubSystem1
    -subSystem2: SubSystem2
    -subSystem3: SubSystem3
    +MethodA(): void
    +MethodB(): void
}

class Client {
    +Main(): void
}

Facade *-- SubSystem1
Facade *-- SubSystem2
Facade *-- SubSystem3

Client -> Facade : uses
Client -.-> SubSystem1 : doesn't access directly
Client -.-> SubSystem2 : doesn't access directly
Client -.-> SubSystem3 : doesn't access directly

note right of Facade
  Facade provides unified
  interface to set of
  interfaces in subsystem
end note

note left of SubSystem1
  Subsystem classes implement
  subsystem functionality
  but have no knowledge
  of facade
end note

note bottom of Client
  Client communicates with
  subsystem only through
  facade interface
end note

@enduml